    title: "歐盟網路安全法案（CRA）：重要與關鍵產品的強制第三方符合性評估機制解析",
    summary: "歐盟網路安全法案（CRA）規定，大多數產品可由製造商自行評估符合性。然而，對於被認定為網路安全角度「重要」或「關鍵」的產品類別，製造商必須透過應用調和標準或接受第三方符合性評估機構（Notified Body）的評估。例如，關鍵產品如智能卡、安全元件、智能電錶閘道器，無論如何都必須接受第三方評估。而「重要」產品（如作業系統、防毒軟體、路由器、防火牆）在製造商未應用調和標準時，也可能強制要求第三方介入。歐盟委員會已透過《實施法規》（Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392）明確指定了產品類別的技術描述。未來，產品若能透過歐盟網路安全認證計畫（EU cybersecurity certification scheme）認證，可能無需第三方參與。此機制強調了成員國在管理符合性評估機構（CABs）中的重要角色。",
    tags: ["CRA", "網路安全法案", "符合性評估", "Notified Body", "實施法規", "歐盟"],
    title_en: "EU Cyber Resilience Act (CRA): Analysis of Mandatory Third-Party Conformity Assessment for Important and Key Products",
    summary_en: "The EU Cyber Resilience Act (CRA) stipulates that most products can undergo self-assessment for conformity by the manufacturer. However, for product categories deemed 'important' or 'key' from a cybersecurity perspective, manufacturers must either apply a harmonized standard or undergo assessment by a Notified Body. For instance, key products such as smart cards, secure elements, and smart meter gateways must undergo third-party assessment regardless. Furthermore, 'important' products (such as operating systems, anti-virus software, routers, and firewalls) may also be mandatorily required to involve third parties if the manufacturer does not apply a harmonized standard. The European Commission has clearly specified the technical descriptions of product categories through the Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392). In the future, products that obtain certification through the EU cybersecurity certification scheme may potentially be exempt from third-party involvement. This mechanism emphasizes the crucial role of Member States in managing Conformity Assessment Bodies (CABs).",
